From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: use BORE's base slice in update_protect_slice()

In 7.3.1, update_protect_slice() starts from
normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice and takes the shortest queued slice only
under RUN_TO_PARITY, as set_protect_slice() does. BORE (CachyOS
kernel-patches 7.3/sched/0001-bore-cachy.patch) declares that variable only
without CONFIG_SCHED_BORE and gives set_protect_slice() sysctl_sched_base_slice
instead, but predates the change, so fair.c no longer builds with it. Do the
same in update_protect_slice().

BORE applies after the device stack, so this goes in before it. Drop it once
BORE covers update_protect_slice().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -1152,7 +1152,11 @@
 static inline void update_protect_slice(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq, struct sched_entity *se)
 {
 	u64 vruntime = min_vruntime(se->vruntime, avg_vruntime(cfs_rq));
+#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+	u64 slice = sysctl_sched_base_slice;
+#else /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 	u64 slice = normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice;
+#endif /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 	u64 vprot;
 
 	if (sched_feat(RUN_TO_PARITY))
